# `sum(a, 1, 2)`, called in a loop, for a callee that adds its arguments up in a for-of: in the copy each step finds its position a known integer and the state holds the list, so the step is the argument.
# No list is made, nothing is read out of one, no loop of the callee is left, and the sum is a sum of integers.
# OPTIONS: check=Validate
# RUN: walk f3 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f3:Body
# CHECK: frame 1 callee=f1
# CHECK-NOT: NewArray
# CHECK-NOT: GetArrayLength
# CHECK-NOT: GetArrayElement
# CHECK: = Add {{*}} form=Integers
# Outside a loop no copy is made for the turns of a for-of: a callee that is too large to be copied for its size is called.
# RUN(ONCE): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# ONCE-LABEL: code f4:Body
# ONCE-NOT: callee=f2
# A for-of of the unit's own body over a list in sight, outside of loops, stays a loop: laid out turn by turn it was a tenth more code on a program of 100,000 lines.
# RUN(OWN): walk f5 mechanisms=all
# OWN-LABEL: code f5:Body
# OWN: LoopHint
# -- source: turns-of-a-for-of-over-the-list-of-a-call-are-written-out-from-source.ts
